WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.899
Film Courage: What came first for you, art
or business?

00:00:02.899 --> 00:00:06.540
Dale Stelly, Filmmaker: It was…it was both
actually.

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:10.030
They came at the same time.

00:00:10.030 --> 00:00:19.210
I was fortunate to have a very close friend
of mine Daniel Zirilli that I did my first

00:00:19.210 --> 00:00:25.550
production job with and I was craft service
or something in like 1995?

00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:33.090
My first job on set was craft service and
was for a very good friend of mine Daniel

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:36.070
Zirilli (he owns the company called Pop Art
Film Factory).

00:00:36.070 --> 00:00:41.940
What I learned from him right off the bat
was he was a director.

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:45.320
Not only was he a director, but he owned the
production company.

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:48.911
So I learned right off the bat if I wanted
to be in this game, I had to be like my friend

00:00:48.911 --> 00:00:49.911
Daniel.

00:00:49.911 --> 00:00:54.260
I’ve got to own the company, I’ve got
to own the production company and then direct.

00:00:54.260 --> 00:00:59.620
So I learned the business before directing
like you have to set up a company.

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:02.970
I set up Stelly Entertainment.

00:01:02.970 --> 00:01:10.080
I PA’d and then I Second AD’d, then First
AD’d 1995 into 1996 and working behind my

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:16.690
friend Daniel being 21 at the time I got envious
of him.

00:01:16.690 --> 00:01:18.800
I’m like “Man, I want to be a director.”

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:24.170
He was older than me and obviously like a
mentor in a way but he didn’t realize that

00:01:24.170 --> 00:01:27.880
I was actually paying attention and sucking
up everything.

00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:32.250
And so after 1996 I developed this attitude
of like “I want to be a director.”

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:36.020
So I’m 21 or 22 talking about I want to
be a music video director.

00:01:36.020 --> 00:01:41.690
I was working at Kodak at the time and being
in the shadow of my friend Daniel Zirilli

00:01:41.690 --> 00:01:45.560
and him kind of bringing me up the ranks like
PA, Second AD to First AD.

00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:52.150
I was first ADing music videos that were on
BET in like 1996 and that’s what kind of

00:01:52.150 --> 00:01:58.930
built up my confidence to start Stelly Entertainment
from a business perspective because if people

00:01:58.930 --> 00:02:02.640
are going to take me seriously I’ve got
to have a production company and then my production

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:07.340
company will loan out my directing services
or my writing services or my producing services

00:02:07.340 --> 00:02:08.340
or whatever.

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:14.020
So in my 20’s I learned right away how to
run a production company to get checks written

00:02:14.020 --> 00:02:17.340
to Stelly Entertainment not to Dale Stelly.

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:23.170
That was a big deal for me and a big step
for me and my company because I worked at

00:02:23.170 --> 00:02:29.690
a post house at the time and I would take
some of my friends out to lunch and then when

00:02:29.690 --> 00:02:34.580
I would put my credit card down it was my
Stelly Entertainment credit card and they’d

00:02:34.580 --> 00:02:37.550
be like “How do you have a Stelly Entertainment
credit card?”

00:02:37.550 --> 00:02:43.010
And I was already starting my business, I
was already doing lunches.

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:48.270
It was bananas because I had already foreseen
me starting my company, I already seen my

00:02:48.270 --> 00:02:49.550
taking my friends out on lunch meetings.

00:02:49.550 --> 00:02:55.810
I had already seen myself buying this car,
seeing my car going on the back lot with my

00:02:55.810 --> 00:02:56.930
“Director” plates.

00:02:56.930 --> 00:03:03.940
I visualized all of this and I made it happen
and in like 2006 or 2007 I am going on the

00:03:03.940 --> 00:03:05.290
back lot of Universal.

00:03:05.290 --> 00:03:09.830
They are letting me in because they know my
car and recognize me.

00:03:09.830 --> 00:03:17.700
Everything I pre-visualized and everything
came to life all the way to me getting an

00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:22.191
office on the back lot not even knowing how
that was going to happen but I knew “I want

00:03:22.191 --> 00:03:24.209
to be on the back lot.”

00:03:24.209 --> 00:03:28.080
And I ended up on the back lot for like a
year and a half with a partner of mine.

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:34.800
But yes, when you believe and you have faith
and you put that in the Universe everyday

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:39.290
you can manifest some unbelievable situations.

00:03:39.290 --> 00:03:42.780
And I like to say me I don’t come from a
rich family.

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:50.379
I just really dedicated myself in figuring
out this movie business, every facet, from

00:03:50.379 --> 00:03:55.370
post production, I worked in post production
for over 13 years so I know exactly what it

00:03:55.370 --> 00:04:02.480
takes to shoot and make a movie for little
money or for huge amounts of money.

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:07.830
And having that talent and skill is very valuable
in this business.

00:04:07.830 --> 00:04:13.209
Because right now with the technology and
everything people are condensing film crews

00:04:13.209 --> 00:04:15.330
to three man, four man.

00:04:15.330 --> 00:04:21.109
And it used to be 25 people crew back in the
day because of the budgets and technologies,

00:04:21.109 --> 00:04:26.020
these millennials they done figured out how
to make projects on cell phones and everything.

00:04:26.020 --> 00:04:32.779
So it’s like you really have got to stay
on top of the creativity and put out the best

00:04:32.779 --> 00:04:37.500
product that you can economically and you’ll
win.

